    rdfs:comment "Technical note: in IFC this property takes 'IfcElectricVoltageMeasure' as value. Such objects are not included in bSDD for simplicity reason. IFC also doesn't enforce particular units, but recommends using metric SI units (metre, kilogram, etc.). Read the IFC documentation for more information." ;
    rdfs:range xsd:decimal ;
    skos:definition "Nominal value of the spark gap breakdown voltage tolerance." ;
    meta:propertyValueKind "Single" ;
    meta:sourceCode "BreakdownVoltageTolerance" .

ifc:BreakerUnitCurve a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "Breaker Unit Curve" ;
    rdfs:comment "Technical note: this is a specific property from IFC that takes a table as its value. That table has two columns (lists), one with definitions and other for defined values. Read the IFC documentation for more information." ;
    rdfs:range xsd:decimal ;
    skos:definition "A curve that establishes the let through energy of a breaker unit when a particular prospective current is applied.A list of minimum 2 and maximum 16 numbers providing the currents in A for points in the current/I2t log/log coordinate space. The curve is drawn as a straight line between two consecutive points.;A list of minimum 2 and maximum 16 numbers providing the let-through energy, I2t, in A2s for points in the current/I2t log/log coordinate space. The curve is drawn as a straight line between two consecutive points." ;
    meta:propertyValueKind "Complex" ;
    meta:sourceCode "BreakerUnitCurve" .

ifc:BreakerUnitFuseBreakingingCurve a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "Breaker Unit Fuse Breakinging Curve" ;
    rdfs:comment "Technical note: this is a specific property from IFC that takes a table as its value. That table has two columns (lists), one with definitions and other for defined values. Read the IFC documentation for more information." ;
    rdfs:range xsd:decimal ;
    skos:definition "A curve that establishes the let through breaking energy of a breaker unit when a particular prospective breaking current is applied.A list of minimum 2 and maximum 8 numbers providing the currents in A for points in the; current/breaking energy log/log coordinate space. The curve is drawn as a straight line between two consecutive points.;A list of minimum 2 and maximum 8 numbers providing the breaking energy whereby the fuse has provided a break, I2t, in A2s for points in the current/breakting_energy log/log coordinate space. The curve is drawn as a straight line between two consecutive." ;
    meta:propertyValueKind "Complex" ;
    meta:sourceCode "BreakerUnitFuseBreakingingCurve" .

ifc:BreakerUnitFuseMeltingCurve a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "Breaker Unit Fuse Melting Curve" ;
    rdfs:comment "Technical note: this is a specific property from IFC that takes a table as its value. That table has two columns (lists), one with definitions and other for defined values. Read the IFC documentation for more information." ;
    rdfs:range xsd:decimal ;
    skos:definition "A curve that establishes the energy required to melt the fuse of a breaker unit when a particular prospective melting current is applied.A list of minimum 2 and maximum 8 numbers providing the currents in A for points in the; current/melting_energy log/log coordinate space. The curve is drawn as a straight line between two consecutive points.;A list of minimum 2 and maximum 8 numbers providing the energy whereby the fuse is starting to melt, I2t, in A2s for points in the current/melting_energy log/log coordinate space. The curve is drawn as a straight line between two consecutive points." ;
    meta:propertyValueKind "Complex" ;
    meta:sourceCode "BreakerUnitFuseMeltingCurve" .

ifc:BreakerUnitIPICurve a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "Breaker Unit Ipi Curve" ;
    rdfs:comment "Technical note: this is a specific property from IFC that takes a table as its value. That table has two columns (lists), one with definitions and other for defined values. Read the IFC documentation for more information." ;
    rdfs:range xsd:decimal ;
    skos:definition "A curve that establishes the let through peak current of a breaker unit when a particular prospective current is applied.A list of minimum 2 and maximum 16 numbers providing the currents in A for points in the I/Î log/log coordinate space. The curve is drawn as a straight line between two consecutive points.;A list of minimum 2 and maximum 16 numbers providing the let-through peak currents, Î, in A for points in the I/Î log/log coordinate space. The curve is drawn as a straight line between two consecutive points." ;
    meta:propertyValueKind "Complex" ;
    meta:sourceCode "BreakerUnitIPICurve" .

ifc:BreakingCapacity a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "Break Ing Capacity" ;
    rdfs:comment "Technical note: in IFC this property takes 'IfcElectricCurrentMeasure' as value. Such objects are not included in bSDD for simplicity reason. IFC also doesn't enforce particular units, but recommends using metric SI units (metre, kilogram, etc.). Read the IFC documentation for more information." ;
