ifc:IfcBuildingElementPartSAFETYCAGE a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Safety Cage" ;
    rdfs:comment "Technical note: Because this class is a 'Predefined Type' in IFC, meaning a specialisation of its parent class, in IFC it should be represented by the parent class." ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ifc:IfcBuildingElementPart ;
    skos:definition "Safety cages are an assembly of circular and vertical bars that are fastened to the stiles of fixed ladders and are arranged to enclose the path of a worker when climbing the ladder. Ladders so enclosed are also known as caged or hooped ladders." ;
