ifc:IfcCurtainWall a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Curtain Wall" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ifc:IfcBuiltElement ;
    skos:definition "A curtain wall is a wall of a building which is an assembly of components, hung from the edge of the floor/roof structure rather than bearing on a floor. Curtain wall is represented as a building element assembly and implemented as a subtype of [[IfcBuiltElement]] that uses an IfcRelAggregates relationship. A curtain wall is often external, but using [[Pset_CurtainWallCommon]].[[IsExternal]] can be used to define interior curtain walls." ;
