ifc:IfcFireSuppressionTerminalBREECHINGINLET a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Breeching Inlet" ;
    rdfs:comment "Technical note: Because this class is a 'Predefined Type' in IFC, meaning a specialisation of its parent class, in IFC it should be represented by the parent class." ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ifc:IfcFireSuppressionTerminal ;
    skos:definition "Symmetrical pipe fitting that unites two or more inlets into a single pipe. A breeching inlet may be used on either a wet or dry riser. Used by fire services personnel for fast connection of fire appliance hose reels. May also be used for foam." ;
