ifc:IfcVibrationDamperRUBBER a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Rubber" ;
    rdfs:comment "Technical note: Because this class is a 'Predefined Type' in IFC, meaning a specialisation of its parent class, in IFC it should be represented by the parent class." ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ifc:IfcVibrationDamper ;
    skos:definition "The rubber mold is a damper that absorbs energy by utilizing deformation of laminated rubber. The difference between the seismic isolation bearing and the rubber type damper is whether or not to support the weight of the upper structures. The rubber damper does not transmit the weight of the upper structures to the sub structure." ;
